{"id": "EUVD-2026-103036", "enisaUuid": "786f23af-e2b2-3550-94e6-8e67007c6da1", "description": "DataCap through 2025.1.1 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in BaseController.getInfoForPath that allows authenticated users to read other users' datasources, snippets and dashboards by numeric id. Low-privileged attackers can enumerate auto-increment ids on the source, snippet and dashboard endpoints to retrieve serialized datasource host, port, username and cleartext passwords.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:38:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T20:37:34", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/metaforge-datacap-source-getbyid-cross-user-idor", "https://github.com/devlive-community/MetaForge/blob/2025.1.1/core/datacap-service/src/main/java/io/edurt/datacap/service/service/BaseService.java#L38-L43", "https://github.com/devlive-community/MetaForge/blob/2025.1.1/core/datacap-server/src/main/java/io/edurt/datacap/server/controller/BaseController.java#L91-L95", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/datacap-through-2025.1.1-idor-via-basecontroller-getinfoforpath-exposes-credentials"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111614", "GHSA-pp2x-5mgr-8c5h"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d93c66f-6c72-32bb-baa3-9e6a59c996f1", "product": {"name": "Datacap", "vendor": {"name": "IBM"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642025.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0eea527d-519c-385f-aa45-c53333201278", "vendor": {"name": "devlive-community"}}], "isExploited": false}